{# Shown while no result records are published: what is compared and measured, no numbers. #}
{% macro links(slugs) -%}
{% for s in nav_systems if s.slug[:-5] in slugs %}<a href="{{ root }}systems/{{ s.slug }}">{{ s.label }}</a>{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}
<section class="card preview">
  <h2>Measurements in progress</h2>
  <p>No results are published yet. The campaigns are running on the reference host; every chart on this site appears
    once the result files are reviewed and added to the repository. Until then this site shows what is compared, how
    each system is configured and how it is measured.</p>
</section>
<section class="card">
  <h2>What is compared</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Systems</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>DuckDB inside the database, ordinary SQL on tables</td>
        <td>{{ links(["alisql", "mariadb", "percona", "pgduckdb", "pgducklake"]) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>DuckDB functions over Parquet files (measured on Parquet entry points)</td><td>{{ links(["villagesql"]) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Reference: plain DuckDB at several versions</td><td>{{ links(["duckdb"]) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Reference: row stores</td><td>{{ links(["innodb", "postgres"]) }}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Each system page lists its versions and image digests, every setting that differs from the default with
    the reason, and how the system is loaded and measured.</p>
</section>
<section class="card">
  <h2>What is measured</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Id</th><th>Measure</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>M1</td><td>Query speed: the 22 TPC-H queries, cold run and median of three warm runs</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M2</td><td>Load time: fastest documented bulk load, and conversion from row-store tables</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M3</td><td>Storage size after load and after a checkpoint</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M4</td><td>Throughput with 1 to 32 concurrent query streams</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M5</td><td>SQL compatibility: a fixed probe suite, each probe classified by what happened</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M6</td><td>Correctness: every result checked against a reference before its time counts</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M7</td><td>Integration overhead: time relative to plain DuckDB at the same DuckDB version</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M8</td><td>Silent slow paths: queries that quietly fall back to row execution</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M9</td><td>Bigger than memory (not yet run)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>M10</td><td>Crash safety during load and commit (not yet run)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">How each measure works, the limits and the tolerances are on the <a href="{{ root }}methodology.html">methodology
    page</a>.</p>
</section>
